.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_EVENT_CALLBACKS 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_event_callbacks ,
.Nm ndi_event_callbacks_t
.Nd internal nexus event callback registration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An \fBndi_event_callbacks_t\fP records a callback registered through
\fBndi_event_add_callback()\fP.
The event framework allocates, links, and frees this structure.
Drivers must use the returned \fBddi_callback_id_t\fP to remove a registration
and must not allocate or modify the structure themselves.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va ndi_evtcb_next , ndi_evtcb_prev
Framework linkage in the event cookie's callback list.
.It Va ndi_evtcb_dip
Device node that registered the callback.
.It Va devname
Driver name recorded for diagnostic output.
.It Va ndi_evtcb_callback
Callback function, invoked with the \fBddi_event_cb_f\fP calling
convention despite the unprototyped pointer in this internal structure.
.It Va ndi_evtcb_arg
Opaque argument supplied by the registrant.
.It Va ndi_evtcb_cookie
Event cookie for this registration.
.El
.Pp
The node, cookie, and callback argument must remain valid while registered.
The framework's callback-list lock protects registration linkage and
serializes removal with event delivery.
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct ndi_event_callbacks *ndi_evtcb_next;
struct ndi_event_callbacks *ndi_evtcb_prev;
dev_info_t                *ndi_evtcb_dip;
char                      *devname;
void                      (*ndi_evtcb_callback)();
void                      *ndi_evtcb_arg;
ddi_eventcookie_t         ndi_evtcb_cookie;
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_event_add_callback 9F ,
.Xr ndi_event_cookie 9S
